# mksite OUTDIR: the Tigris website, a directory of static pages built
#                 from the tree with sh and awk alone, for GitHub Pages
#                 (.github/workflows/pages.yml publishes it on a release):
#
#   index.html          README.md
#   json-format.html    doc/json-format.md, the JSON report's contract
#   metadata.html       doc/metadata.md, the finding metadata format
#   findings/           every finding id, by category, with a filter, and
#                       a page per id: severity, category, the checks that
#                       report it, the fix, references, controls, the text
#   compliance/         a page per framework: each control, and the ids
#                       that are evidence about it
#   schema/, art/       the JSON Schema and the artwork, as they are
#
#   The markdown is a subset, the one the README and docs use: headings
#   with GitHub's anchors, fenced code, tables, lists, raw HTML blocks,
#   paragraphs; code spans, bold, italics, links, images. A link to a file
#   the site does not carry goes to it on GitHub. tests/site_check.sh
#   builds it and follows every link.
#
#-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
out=${1:-}
[ -n "$out" ] || { echo "usage: mksite OUTDIR" >&2; exit 2; }
case "$out" in /*) ;; *) out=`pwd`/$out ;; esac
T=`cd "\`dirname "$0"\`/.." && pwd`
